Thus assert: bitIndex >= 0 => this.get(bitIndex) == value;

But we need to refer to method get defined earlier: public boolean get(int bitIndex). So we can use this.get(bitIndex). The implication is if bitIndex >=0 then after operation, get(bitIndex) equals value. It doesn't mention other bits unaffected.

Thus final assert: assert bitIndex >= 0 => this.get(bitIndex) == value;

